<article class="env-lemma" id="018T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/018T">Lemma <span data-tag="018T">14.21.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category Let $U$ be an $m$-truncated simplicial object of $\mathcal{A}$. For $n > m$ we have $N(i_{m!}U)_ n = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $V = i_{m!}U$. Let $V' \subset V$ be the simplicial subobject of $V$ with $V'_ i = V_ i$ for $i \leq m$ and $N(V'_ i) = 0$ for $i > m$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/017Y" data-tag="017Y">14.18.9</a>. By the adjunction formula, since $\text{sk}_ m V' = U$, there is an inverse to the injection $V' \to V$. Hence $V' = V$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>